1
00:00:05,100 --> 00:00:07,680
Open the door! Let me out of here!

2
00:00:07,680 --> 00:00:09,150
Open the door!

3
00:00:11,680 --> 00:00:13,280
It's too late.

4
00:00:14,440 --> 00:00:16,280
It is <i>not</i> too late!

5
00:00:16,280 --> 00:00:17,950
I have to get to Rem right now!

6
00:00:17,950 --> 00:00:20,660
Your reason for returning to that room

7
00:00:20,660 --> 00:00:22,780
has just disappeared, I suppose.

8
00:00:35,740 --> 00:00:38,470
To hell with that!

9
00:00:41,120 --> 00:00:44,630
Why are you trying to save me?!

10
00:00:45,480 --> 00:00:48,520
Because you look so pathetic, 
I can't bear the sight of you.

11
00:00:49,120 --> 00:00:51,160
But why me?!

12
00:00:51,160 --> 00:00:52,990
If you really want to save someone,

13
00:00:53,530 --> 00:00:55,030
why don't you save them?!

14
00:00:55,410 --> 00:00:57,640
You could have done it!

15
00:00:57,640 --> 00:01:00,740
Wh-Why should I have to do that?

16
00:01:01,470 --> 00:01:05,850
I haven't a single reason 
to save anyone, I suppose.

17
00:01:05,850 --> 00:01:09,960
Then... you have no reason 
to save me, either!

18
00:01:10,530 --> 00:01:13,830
Who asked you to save me?!

19
00:01:15,890 --> 00:01:18,880
Do you have any idea what you've done?!

20
00:01:18,880 --> 00:01:22,310
Everything might be ruined now, because of you!

21
00:01:22,310 --> 00:01:23,890
Everything will be rewritten,

22
00:01:24,240 --> 00:01:26,930
and this horrible present 
will be set in stone!

23
00:01:27,640 --> 00:01:30,820
You should have just killed me!

24
00:01:35,270 --> 00:01:36,150
I don't understand.

25
00:01:37,570 --> 00:01:38,860
I don't understand!

26
00:01:39,770 --> 00:01:40,950
Fine, then.

27
00:01:41,250 --> 00:01:43,870
If you're not going to help, then...

28
00:01:46,410 --> 00:01:47,120
No!

29
00:01:50,110 --> 00:01:51,840
Why... are you...

30
00:01:51,840 --> 00:01:53,520
I won't let you, I suppose!

31
00:01:53,520 --> 00:01:55,660
I won't let you die here!

32
00:01:55,660 --> 00:01:57,510
Let me go right now!

33
00:02:09,760 --> 00:02:12,830
Why... is that here?

34
00:02:24,720 --> 00:02:25,450
Why?

35
00:02:26,600 --> 00:02:30,710
Why are you holding that 
book like it's so precious?

36
00:02:32,070 --> 00:02:36,940
That's not the same book the 
Witch Cultists had... is it?

37
00:02:37,880 --> 00:02:39,820
It only looks like one, right?

38
00:02:41,150 --> 00:02:44,850
Why aren't you denying it?

39
00:02:45,900 --> 00:02:50,060
I haven't been commanded 
to answer that question.

40
00:02:51,190 --> 00:02:53,430
What's written in that book?

41
00:02:53,800 --> 00:02:55,010
What's it telling you to do?

42
00:02:55,010 --> 00:02:57,320
That question isn't in the 
book either, I suppose.

43
00:02:57,800 --> 00:03:00,540
Are you not allowed to do anything 
that's not in the book?!

44
00:03:00,540 --> 00:03:03,200
Then when you gave me cover earlier—

45
00:03:03,200 --> 00:03:05,350
That question isn't here, either.

46
00:03:05,350 --> 00:03:07,810
Then why are you talking to me right now?!

47
00:03:07,810 --> 00:03:09,900
Why did you save me from death's door?!

48
00:03:09,900 --> 00:03:10,620
I don't know!

49
00:03:10,900 --> 00:03:15,800
Are you saying you can't do anything 
that's not written in that book?!

50
00:03:15,800 --> 00:03:17,100
Yes, I suppose!

51
00:03:17,600 --> 00:03:18,740
That's right.

52
00:03:19,240 --> 00:03:22,800
Everything I do is in accordance with 
the Gospel's guidance, I suppose!

53
00:03:23,240 --> 00:03:25,880
That is the meaning of my life!

54
00:03:25,880 --> 00:03:28,420
That is the purpose of my existence!

55
00:03:29,140 --> 00:03:34,480
Did you try to save me because 
the book told you to?

56
00:03:34,480 --> 00:03:36,720
And when you saved me after I'd been cursed,

57
00:03:36,720 --> 00:03:39,240
and when you helped me when 
I couldn't even stand up?!

58
00:03:39,630 --> 00:03:43,140
And when we goofed off, yelled at 
each other, acted like dorks together—

59
00:03:43,140 --> 00:03:44,280
I told you!

60
00:03:44,590 --> 00:03:46,710
Yes, that is why, I suppose!

61
00:03:46,710 --> 00:03:50,520
Everything I've done, everything I've seen,
 everything I've said...

62
00:03:50,520 --> 00:03:53,280
All of it was written in this book!

63
00:03:53,280 --> 00:03:57,260
As if you ever could have moved 
my heart on your own, I suppose!

64
00:03:57,260 --> 00:03:59,300
Don't be so full of yourself, human!

65
00:03:59,640 --> 00:04:02,550
Everything I do is for Mother!

66
00:04:02,550 --> 00:04:04,500
You are just... You are just...

67
00:04:05,020 --> 00:04:06,260
A human! A human!

68
00:04:06,600 --> 00:04:07,260
A human!

69
00:04:16,540 --> 00:04:18,660
Don't touch me, human!

70
00:04:18,660 --> 00:04:20,950
I don't even know you, I suppose, human!

71
00:04:20,950 --> 00:04:22,490
I hate you! I hate you!

72
00:04:22,660 --> 00:04:24,180
I <i>hate</i> you!

73
00:04:31,300 --> 00:04:35,090
Back then... I was so happy...

74
00:04:38,870 --> 00:04:40,380
What a shame.

75
00:04:49,520 --> 00:04:50,280
Oh?

76
00:04:50,280 --> 00:04:52,200
...ea...tri...

77
00:04:53,490 --> 00:04:56,650
How wonderful. He truly cares about you.

78
00:05:22,160 --> 00:05:23,460
Emilia...

79
00:05:29,420 --> 00:05:32,110
My restart point hasn't changed.

80
00:05:32,870 --> 00:05:34,480
This is the third time.

81
00:05:36,410 --> 00:05:37,280
Emilia!

82
00:05:37,280 --> 00:05:40,600
No... You're wrong! It wasn't me!

83
00:05:38,600 --> 00:05:40,900
Emilia! Stay strong!

84
00:05:40,600 --> 00:05:43,340
Help me, Puck... Puck...

85
00:05:40,900 --> 00:05:41,830
Emilia!

86
00:05:42,230 --> 00:05:43,350
Emilia!

87
00:05:48,100 --> 00:05:49,220
Subaru...

88
00:06:07,500 --> 00:06:09,250
I'm sorry, Subaru,

89
00:06:09,670 --> 00:06:11,850
for losing my composure like that.

90
00:06:12,090 --> 00:06:13,970
Hey, it's fine.

91
00:06:14,480 --> 00:06:16,090
But I...

92
00:06:16,680 --> 00:06:19,650
Just rest for tonight. We can talk tomorrow.

93
00:06:22,090 --> 00:06:22,790
Right...

94
00:06:25,440 --> 00:06:27,870
Ram, take care of Emilia.

95
00:06:34,700 --> 00:06:37,230
All that's left is to talk to Roswaal.

96
00:06:37,230 --> 00:06:40,920
I've gotta make sure to ask him about 
Beatrice this time, since I couldn't last time.

97
00:06:38,940 --> 00:06:40,220
Natsuki-san?

98
00:06:40,920 --> 00:06:43,000
Natsuki-san, are you listening?

99
00:06:41,880 --> 00:06:43,000
And... oh?

100
00:06:43,520 --> 00:06:45,750
Natsuki-san, are you all right?

101
00:06:45,750 --> 00:06:46,340
Huh?

102
00:06:46,930 --> 00:06:50,950
Yeah, of course! I'm just great!
 Perfect, in fact!

103
00:06:50,950 --> 00:06:52,950
Does anything look off to you?

104
00:06:53,480 --> 00:06:56,250
No, nothing looks off at all.

105
00:06:56,250 --> 00:06:58,280
You appear very calm.

106
00:06:58,280 --> 00:06:59,810
Right? So—

107
00:06:59,810 --> 00:07:02,720
Even with Emilia-sama in her current state.

108
00:07:03,540 --> 00:07:06,730
So am I wrong to find your 
calmness concerning?

109
00:07:08,390 --> 00:07:12,440
You think... I'm too calm right now?

110
00:07:12,440 --> 00:07:15,530
Yes. I don't think that's a bad thing.

111
00:07:15,720 --> 00:07:16,500
But...

112
00:07:18,740 --> 00:07:22,080
No, thanks to you, I'm more confident now.

113
00:07:22,080 --> 00:07:23,420
Thanks, Otto.

114
00:07:23,800 --> 00:07:24,590
Huh?

115
00:07:24,590 --> 00:07:26,240
That proves I can still

116
00:07:26,240 --> 00:07:29,550
think rationally about things, 
even after all that's happened.

117
00:07:29,550 --> 00:07:34,460
No, but... There's a huge 
difference between looking calm

118
00:07:34,460 --> 00:07:38,190
and being able to think about 
things rationally, in my opinion...

119
00:07:38,190 --> 00:07:40,650
This is Roswaal we're talking about.

120
00:07:40,650 --> 00:07:43,160
I can't let him keep dodging 
the subject this time.

121
00:07:43,560 --> 00:07:45,150
Yo, got a sec?

122
00:07:45,710 --> 00:07:47,060
Garfiel?

123
00:07:47,710 --> 00:07:50,850
You're not one to fall into 
patterns easily, huh?

124
00:07:50,850 --> 00:07:51,620
What?

125
00:07:51,620 --> 00:07:55,830
I mean, last time, you would've gone 
straight back if I hadn't stopped you.

126
00:07:55,830 --> 00:07:57,950
I've got something important to do, y'know.

127
00:07:58,240 --> 00:08:01,840
Huh? You talkin' about your 
shady scheme with that bastard?

128
00:08:01,840 --> 00:08:04,160
Don't call it a shady scheme!

129
00:08:04,160 --> 00:08:05,650
So, what'd you want?

130
00:08:05,650 --> 00:08:07,210
Is it about the Sanctuary?

131
00:08:07,630 --> 00:08:11,340
What the hell else d'you think 
I'd wanna talk to you about?

132
00:08:11,980 --> 00:08:14,970
Well, you might want some info on Ram.

133
00:08:14,970 --> 00:08:18,030
She prefers tall guys who 
wear clown makeup—

134
00:08:18,030 --> 00:08:21,020
Cut it out! You're depressing me!

135
00:08:21,480 --> 00:08:25,240
So on that note, we're gonna 
go chat about our love lives!

136
00:08:25,240 --> 00:08:26,520
Natsuki-san... But...

137
00:08:27,030 --> 00:08:29,610
C'mon, Otto. Save it for tomorrow, okay?

138
00:08:30,030 --> 00:08:32,300
A-All right, fine.

139
00:08:32,300 --> 00:08:36,140
I'll be counting on you to deal 
with the margrave tomorrow.

140
00:08:41,160 --> 00:08:43,460
This ain't the place. Follow me.

141
00:08:44,740 --> 00:08:47,460
Another change in the course of events?

142
00:08:55,560 --> 00:08:56,920
So...

143
00:08:56,920 --> 00:08:59,530
How long has it been since 
you last saw Frederica?

144
00:08:59,530 --> 00:09:03,230
And why the hell should I have to tell you that?

145
00:09:03,560 --> 00:09:05,760
I just thought it couldn't hurt to ask.

146
00:09:05,760 --> 00:09:08,690
Hah! She already left this place.

147
00:09:09,110 --> 00:09:10,480
She ain't none of my concern anymore.

148
00:09:10,840 --> 00:09:12,280
That's the thing.

149
00:09:12,280 --> 00:09:15,120
I know you're Frederica's brother,

150
00:09:15,120 --> 00:09:18,530
which means she meets the 
mixed-blood requirement, too.

151
00:09:18,530 --> 00:09:20,200
So why isn't she here?

152
00:09:20,480 --> 00:09:22,070
Why ask me?

153
00:09:22,070 --> 00:09:25,000
The barrier won't open unless 
someone passes the trial.

154
00:09:25,000 --> 00:09:26,160
Nothing's gonna change that.

155
00:09:26,500 --> 00:09:28,860
Knowing why will give us more options.

156
00:09:29,340 --> 00:09:31,800
I'm the type that wants to have

157
00:09:31,800 --> 00:09:34,800
all the information before 
I rack my brain for answers.

158
00:09:36,690 --> 00:09:37,750
We're here.

159
00:09:50,630 --> 00:09:53,110
You're the one who wanted 
to talk to me, Ryuzu-san?

160
00:09:53,110 --> 00:09:55,900
You may interpret it that way if you wish.

161
00:09:55,900 --> 00:09:58,300
Young Gar is my attendant, after all.

162
00:10:00,360 --> 00:10:02,840
Is this where you come to relax or something?

163
00:10:02,840 --> 00:10:05,220
If you invited me to a place like that,

164
00:10:05,220 --> 00:10:07,910
are you going to start sharing 
your secrets with me soon?

165
00:10:08,320 --> 00:10:10,880
What a smooth talker you are.

166
00:10:11,410 --> 00:10:15,540
So? Are you going to answer 
my question for me?

167
00:10:16,120 --> 00:10:19,800
You mean the reason why Frederica 
left the Sanctuary?

168
00:10:19,800 --> 00:10:23,010
What do you intend to do with that information?

169
00:10:23,320 --> 00:10:27,350
I'll use it to get everyone 
out of the Sanctuary.

170
00:10:27,790 --> 00:10:30,400
Then no one will have to 
undergo the trial, right?

171
00:10:30,700 --> 00:10:33,240
Logically speaking, yes, you are right.

172
00:10:33,240 --> 00:10:36,210
But why are you so obstinate 
about avoiding the trial?

173
00:10:36,210 --> 00:10:38,930
Because I don't want to force 
Emilia to go through it.

174
00:10:38,930 --> 00:10:41,490
It's my own purely selfish reason.

175
00:10:43,920 --> 00:10:46,440
That may work for the trial,

176
00:10:46,440 --> 00:10:49,920
but it does not do to constantly 
run away from hardship—

177
00:10:49,920 --> 00:10:52,210
I'm not talking about running away.

178
00:10:52,880 --> 00:10:56,680
It may not be now, but Emilia will 
eventually have to face her past.

179
00:10:57,330 --> 00:10:59,040
You want to give her an escape,

180
00:10:59,040 --> 00:11:03,100
but not from the things that 
will hurt her the most?

181
00:11:03,720 --> 00:11:05,940
She'll beat it without running away.

182
00:11:06,350 --> 00:11:09,340
I have complete faith that the girl 
I fell for can pull that off.

183
00:11:13,670 --> 00:11:15,420
Tell 'im, old hag!

184
00:11:15,900 --> 00:11:20,120
Tell 'im it's just like a gadgy gwadzeadd 
tryin' to hide in the mountains!

185
00:11:20,120 --> 00:11:23,640
I appreciate it, but I have 
no idea what you just said.

186
00:11:23,640 --> 00:11:28,620
What Young Gar is trying to say is that 
there is no convenient path by which to escape.

187
00:11:28,930 --> 00:11:32,960
Frederica's exit was 
something of an exception.

188
00:11:32,960 --> 00:11:36,840
She does not meet the conditions 
for being held within the barrier.

189
00:11:37,410 --> 00:11:39,820
Conditions to be held within the barrier?

190
00:11:39,820 --> 00:11:42,230
So there's something else 
besides being half?

191
00:11:42,230 --> 00:11:44,680
No, there are no exceptions.

192
00:11:44,680 --> 00:11:45,710
Then...

193
00:11:45,710 --> 00:11:48,520
The barrier determines one's 
mixed-blood status by the amount

194
00:11:48,520 --> 00:11:50,240
of each race in their blood.

195
00:11:50,240 --> 00:11:52,840
If they possess human and non-human 
blood in equal amounts,

196
00:11:52,840 --> 00:11:54,540
they will be held within the barrier.

197
00:11:55,200 --> 00:11:56,420
However...

198
00:11:56,420 --> 00:11:58,080
If you're less than a half-blood...

199
00:11:58,080 --> 00:12:00,190
like, a quarter-blood or something, 
it can't hold you?

200
00:12:00,960 --> 00:12:02,280
That means...

201
00:12:02,280 --> 00:12:04,030
We have different dads.

202
00:12:04,680 --> 00:12:07,260
I'm Garfiel Tinzel.

203
00:12:08,120 --> 00:12:11,250
I'm pretty sure she uses a different surname.

204
00:12:11,550 --> 00:12:13,460
I am Frederica Baumann.

205
00:12:15,150 --> 00:12:18,590
She was born to a human mother 
and a mixed-blood father.

206
00:12:19,090 --> 00:12:21,920
Therefore, she can enter and 
leave the forest at will.

207
00:12:22,340 --> 00:12:24,600
Hah! Enter and leave at will?

208
00:12:24,600 --> 00:12:25,890
Don't make me laugh!

209
00:12:25,890 --> 00:12:29,330
She hasn't been back here in over ten years!

210
00:12:29,330 --> 00:12:31,180
Frederica abandoned this place!

211
00:12:32,370 --> 00:12:33,680
Young Gar...

212
00:12:34,880 --> 00:12:36,800
And now you know.

213
00:12:36,800 --> 00:12:40,820
I apologize for making you listen 
so long to learn so little.

214
00:12:41,240 --> 00:12:42,420
Nah.

215
00:12:42,420 --> 00:12:46,940
It's a lot better than just being 
stuck with unusable options forever.

216
00:12:47,370 --> 00:12:50,160
But I guess we still have 
to pass the trial, then...

217
00:12:52,590 --> 00:12:55,270
Garfiel, Ryuzu-san...

218
00:12:55,270 --> 00:12:57,380
I'd like to offer a suggestion.

219
00:12:58,190 --> 00:12:59,840
A suggestion, eh?

220
00:13:00,200 --> 00:13:04,530
I'm on my way to get Roswaal 
and Emilia on board with this,

221
00:13:04,530 --> 00:13:08,240
but it's really important, so I'd appreciate 
it if you wouldn't tell anyone.

222
00:13:10,530 --> 00:13:13,650
Very well. We will tell no one.

223
00:13:13,650 --> 00:13:15,270
Tell us whatever you wish.

224
00:13:17,460 --> 00:13:20,150
I want to undergo the trial in Emilia's place.

225
00:13:20,420 --> 00:13:21,400
Huh?!

226
00:13:21,760 --> 00:13:23,780
When I entered the graveyard to help Emilia,

227
00:13:24,300 --> 00:13:25,570
I came back unharmed, right?

228
00:13:26,000 --> 00:13:28,870
That's because I have the qualification 
to undergo the trial.

229
00:13:29,160 --> 00:13:31,910
On top of that, I've already 
passed one of them.

230
00:13:32,380 --> 00:13:33,870
You passed the trial?!

231
00:13:35,580 --> 00:13:37,880
"Things have gotten complicated."

232
00:13:37,880 --> 00:13:39,330
Is that what you're thinking, Ryuzu-san?

233
00:13:39,920 --> 00:13:44,190
I cannot deny that you took the 
very words out of my mouth.

234
00:13:44,600 --> 00:13:47,690
But I now understand your point.

235
00:13:51,350 --> 00:13:55,250
Young Su, there is something important 
I must tell you, too.

236
00:13:55,250 --> 00:13:55,930
What?

237
00:13:56,360 --> 00:14:01,650
Right now, I need you to keep 
quiet and behave yourself.

238
00:14:01,880 --> 00:14:02,550
Huh?

239
00:14:05,620 --> 00:14:08,830
I know you must be wondering 
why this is happening.

240
00:14:08,830 --> 00:14:11,580
But I will not ask your forgiveness.

241
00:14:11,580 --> 00:14:14,790
As promised, I will tell 
no one what you told me.

242
00:14:14,790 --> 00:14:17,780
I swear it on the name of Ryuzu Shima.

243
00:14:30,990 --> 00:14:32,620
You awake now?

244
00:14:34,810 --> 00:14:36,310
I'll untie ya.

245
00:14:36,310 --> 00:14:39,540
And just so ya know, it ain't 
no use cryin' for help.

246
00:14:40,200 --> 00:14:41,540
Someone help!

247
00:14:41,540 --> 00:14:43,300
I just said it won't work!

248
00:14:43,300 --> 00:14:45,990
This is a part of the Sanctuary 
no one knows about!

249
00:14:48,240 --> 00:14:52,740
Ain't no need to save someone 
who wants to die, right?

250
00:14:53,040 --> 00:14:55,070
I don't know what you're talking about!

251
00:14:55,070 --> 00:14:59,360
You guys are pretty famous for 
being a bunch of weirdos.

252
00:14:59,360 --> 00:15:01,960
Wait... I seriously don't get...

253
00:15:01,960 --> 00:15:03,240
Don't play dumb!

254
00:15:03,240 --> 00:15:06,440
There's miasma oozin' out 
of every pore in your body!

255
00:15:06,440 --> 00:15:07,460
You're a witch cultist!

256
00:15:08,760 --> 00:15:12,410
The smell's been stronger since 
you came outta the graveyard.

257
00:15:12,990 --> 00:15:15,760
Not many people have this much miasma.

258
00:15:16,160 --> 00:15:19,540
So I was gonna let you go if you 
swore you wouldn't try anything,

259
00:15:19,540 --> 00:15:22,620
but you say you wanna undergo the 
trial in the princess's place?

260
00:15:22,620 --> 00:15:23,990
That ain't no joke!

261
00:15:25,080 --> 00:15:28,780
You can smell... the witch's scent on me?

262
00:15:28,960 --> 00:15:31,700
Hah! That's a funny thing to call it!

263
00:15:32,200 --> 00:15:35,300
It just fits, don't it? "The witch's scent"!

264
00:15:35,780 --> 00:15:38,140
What is it you wanna do in that graveyard?!

265
00:15:38,760 --> 00:15:40,150
What're you planning?

266
00:15:40,150 --> 00:15:43,400
Can't be anything good if the 
witch's tomb is part of it.

267
00:15:43,400 --> 00:15:46,800
Why trap me in here, then?

268
00:15:46,800 --> 00:15:48,600
Why not kill me?

269
00:15:48,600 --> 00:15:52,840
Hah! 'Cause you have a way 
of winnin' people over!

270
00:15:53,520 --> 00:15:59,230
I don't wanna kill you and have it blow up 
in my face like the fall of the Tesla Fortress!

271
00:15:59,230 --> 00:16:01,100
Then what are you gonna do with me?

272
00:16:01,400 --> 00:16:05,080
For now, I'll just say it's 
all up to Emilia-sama.

273
00:16:13,990 --> 00:16:15,590
Not happening!

274
00:16:15,590 --> 00:16:17,320
I won't let you kill yourself, either!

275
00:16:17,320 --> 00:16:20,980
I don't have a damn clue what you're thinking,

276
00:16:21,390 --> 00:16:25,790
but what pisses me off more than 
anything is that attitude of yours!

277
00:16:25,790 --> 00:16:29,800
Your eyes look just like that 
Roswaal bastard's eyes!

278
00:16:29,800 --> 00:16:32,650
Don't you dare try anything funny!

279
00:16:38,950 --> 00:16:40,450
Subaru-sama!

280
00:16:40,450 --> 00:16:41,910
Subaru-sama!

281
00:16:43,360 --> 00:16:45,060
Subaru!

282
00:16:52,160 --> 00:16:53,530
Ram, anything?

283
00:16:54,160 --> 00:16:55,640
Sadly, no.

284
00:16:55,640 --> 00:17:01,010
Anyone who wanders into the Lost Forest at 
night alone ain't gonna make it back easy.

285
00:17:01,010 --> 00:17:02,000
Alone?

286
00:17:03,960 --> 00:17:05,290
N-Never mind.

287
00:17:05,760 --> 00:17:09,380
Puck, why won't you come out?

288
00:17:10,060 --> 00:17:12,340
Hey, bro. Come with me for a sec.

289
00:17:12,340 --> 00:17:12,940
Huh?!

290
00:17:15,310 --> 00:17:17,770
Don't you go runnin' your mouth.

291
00:17:17,770 --> 00:17:19,390
As long as you don't...

292
00:17:28,960 --> 00:17:31,880
<i>He tied me up way too tight!</i>

293
00:17:38,280 --> 00:17:42,000
<i>I don't have time to waste stuck in here!</i>

294
00:17:42,000 --> 00:17:44,610
<i>Think. What I know right now</i>

295
00:17:44,610 --> 00:17:48,540
<i>is that whoever's attacking the mansion will 
wait until someone arrives back there.</i>

296
00:17:48,540 --> 00:17:50,630
<i>As of now, the longest it's been was five days.</i>

297
00:17:53,910 --> 00:17:55,780
Beatrice...

298
00:17:55,780 --> 00:17:59,800
<i>Have you really just been following 
the Gospel's commands all this time?</i>

299
00:18:00,230 --> 00:18:00,850
I told you!

300
00:18:01,080 --> 00:18:02,850
Yes, that is why, I suppose!

301
00:18:04,160 --> 00:18:06,070
<i>Even if that's true...</i>

302
00:18:06,980 --> 00:18:10,620
<i>I would give anything to 
hear your voice right now.</i>

303
00:19:27,470 --> 00:19:30,280
I suspected you would be in a miserable state,

304
00:19:30,280 --> 00:19:32,920
but this is even worse than I thought.

305
00:19:34,300 --> 00:19:36,530
Oh, you need to keep quiet.

306
00:19:37,200 --> 00:19:39,640
I'm walking a dangerous tightrope here.

307
00:19:39,640 --> 00:19:41,980
I don't want the lookout catching me now.

308
00:19:42,400 --> 00:19:45,120
You and I both never know 
when to quit, do we?

309
00:19:48,740 --> 00:19:53,350
In any case, I'm relieved you're 
still alive, Natsuki-san.

310
00:19:58,530 --> 00:20:00,050
How long has it been?

311
00:20:00,050 --> 00:20:01,700
Three days.

312
00:20:01,700 --> 00:20:04,600
It's nighttime... and time for the trial.

313
00:20:04,600 --> 00:20:05,770
Three days?!

314
00:20:05,770 --> 00:20:08,740
And the trial is still going on?

315
00:20:08,740 --> 00:20:11,620
Emilia-sama has a plan in mind.

316
00:20:12,110 --> 00:20:14,960
What has happened while I've been away?

317
00:20:14,960 --> 00:20:17,320
Word of your disappearance spread quickly,

318
00:20:17,320 --> 00:20:19,410
causing panic throughout the community.

319
00:20:20,130 --> 00:20:22,990
Emilia-sama has especially 
struggled to keep her composure.

320
00:20:22,990 --> 00:20:26,070
She actually declined to attempt 
the trial the next day.

321
00:20:26,600 --> 00:20:27,830
Emilia?

322
00:20:28,220 --> 00:20:32,010
Everyone has been looking all 
over for you, but with no luck.

323
00:20:32,410 --> 00:20:36,080
So the margrave told Emilia-sama 
that they should prioritize

324
00:20:36,610 --> 00:20:41,680
the liberation of the Sanctuary, so that
 a search party can be assembled.

325
00:20:41,680 --> 00:20:43,140
A search party?

326
00:20:43,680 --> 00:20:45,750
Did Emilia agree to that?

327
00:20:45,750 --> 00:20:49,450
She said the margrave gave her 
some sort of formal oath...

328
00:20:50,420 --> 00:20:55,220
So Emilia has desperately attempted 
the trial again yesterday and today,

329
00:20:55,960 --> 00:21:00,240
and it seems she's deeply despondent 
as her attempts continue to fail.

330
00:21:00,790 --> 00:21:03,770
There's one thing that keeps bothering me...

331
00:21:03,770 --> 00:21:04,450
What is it?

332
00:21:04,860 --> 00:21:09,400
Well... why do you keep talking as 
if you heard all this secondhand?

333
00:21:09,400 --> 00:21:11,950
Oh... You're asking about that?

334
00:21:12,440 --> 00:21:14,800
It's rather hard to say this, honestly...

335
00:21:15,320 --> 00:21:19,300
The truth is... Garfiel also has his eye on me,

336
00:21:19,300 --> 00:21:22,400
so I've been running all around 
trying to avoid him, too.

337
00:21:22,400 --> 00:21:23,140
What?

338
00:21:23,520 --> 00:21:26,830
I was there the last time you 
two saw each other, remember?

339
00:21:27,800 --> 00:21:29,520
It's natural that he'd suspect me.

340
00:21:29,520 --> 00:21:31,990
And then he said to me...

341
00:21:31,990 --> 00:21:37,410
that if I didn't tell anyone you had 
met with him, he wouldn't hurt me.

342
00:21:38,020 --> 00:21:40,900
He showed me what looked like 
a glowing stone as collateral.

343
00:21:40,900 --> 00:21:43,310
And you turned that down?!

344
00:21:43,310 --> 00:21:44,460
Ow...

345
00:21:44,980 --> 00:21:48,240
And now Garfiel's after you?

346
00:21:48,240 --> 00:21:52,490
Yes, so I picked up all this 
information while on the run.

347
00:21:52,490 --> 00:21:54,280
I did hear it secondhand.

348
00:21:54,280 --> 00:21:57,080
Though it's pretty funny how 
long it got drawn out,

349
00:21:57,080 --> 00:21:58,960
considering this was the funner option.

350
00:21:59,260 --> 00:22:01,520
Quit picking on me! Are you insane?!

351
00:22:01,520 --> 00:22:03,310
Why did you do that?!

352
00:22:04,710 --> 00:22:07,850
I really am grateful that 
you came to save me.

353
00:22:08,520 --> 00:22:13,450
Frankly, until I saw your face, I was 
thinking I'd be better off dead.

354
00:22:14,210 --> 00:22:14,890
But...

355
00:22:16,050 --> 00:22:19,100
I can't see why you would help me.

356
00:22:24,560 --> 00:22:26,780
Listen, Natsuki-san...

357
00:22:27,800 --> 00:22:30,310
Is it really such a strange thing

358
00:22:30,870 --> 00:22:33,120
to try to help a friend?

359
00:22:35,800 --> 00:22:36,620
Huh?

360
00:22:38,400 --> 00:22:42,700
Wh-Why are you standing there like 
a statue with such a shocked face?

361
00:22:43,050 --> 00:22:46,650
Well, you just brought up someone 
I don't know out of the blue.

362
00:22:46,650 --> 00:22:48,940
I don't, um... know who "Eugene" is...

363
00:22:48,940 --> 00:22:51,890
You got every single part of that wrong!

364
00:22:51,890 --> 00:22:55,790
I didn't say "Eugene"! I said "friend"!
You know, <i>friend</i>!

365
00:22:55,790 --> 00:22:58,800
Friend? Who is whose friend?

366
00:22:58,800 --> 00:23:00,770
<i>You</i> are<i> my</i> friend!

367
00:23:04,770 --> 00:23:08,860
I mean, it's true that I came here with 
you because it served my interests, too!

368
00:23:09,150 --> 00:23:12,430
First there was the oil, then you 
saved me from the Witch's Cult,

369
00:23:12,430 --> 00:23:15,260
and then there was promise of getting me an 
audience with the margrave...

370
00:23:15,260 --> 00:23:16,200
But...

371
00:23:16,480 --> 00:23:18,410
When you take all those 
favors out of the picture,

372
00:23:18,900 --> 00:23:22,510
I just think of you as a friend, Natsuki-san.

373
00:23:22,960 --> 00:23:26,440
Though I'm not very fond 
of the way you treat me...

374
00:23:26,440 --> 00:23:29,430
But I figure that's just how 
close we are as friends.

375
00:23:34,640 --> 00:23:35,320
What?

376
00:23:37,680 --> 00:23:41,320
Fr... Fr... Friends?! Friends, really?!

377
00:23:41,320 --> 00:23:46,610
I get it now! Otto, you wanted 
to be friends with me?!

378
00:23:49,360 --> 00:23:52,840
Friends... Oh, damn it... 
Otto, I swear, man...

379
00:23:52,840 --> 00:23:54,780
Ouch! That hurts!

380
00:23:55,940 --> 00:23:57,330
What are you doing?!

381
00:23:57,330 --> 00:23:59,980
Okay, fine! I was stupid to even say it!

382
00:23:59,980 --> 00:24:03,120
I knew you would laugh at me!

383
00:24:03,120 --> 00:24:05,960
Well, I mean... how could I not laugh?

384
00:24:05,960 --> 00:24:07,850
You're not the one who's crazy.

385
00:24:07,850 --> 00:24:10,410
I'm just floored by my own stupidity.

386
00:24:10,410 --> 00:24:12,840
I'm so exasperated with myself, I have to laugh!

387
00:24:21,620 --> 00:24:22,700
Natsuki-san?

388
00:24:26,460 --> 00:24:27,880
Sorry.

389
00:24:27,880 --> 00:24:31,190
You really are my friend, Otto.

390
00:24:33,690 --> 00:24:36,780
Thanks for coming to save me.

391
00:24:36,780 --> 00:24:40,040
Friend

392
00:25:52,600 --> 00:25:54,960
Garfiel is at the graveyard right now,

393
00:25:54,960 --> 00:25:57,180
so we can get you out of the barrier.

394
00:25:58,220 --> 00:26:00,660
But the question is whether 
that's even possible.

395
00:26:00,910 --> 00:26:03,820
No need to worry about that.

396
00:26:03,820 --> 00:26:06,240
I have a very reliable helper lined up.

397
00:26:06,240 --> 00:26:07,520
A helper?

398
00:26:12,490 --> 00:26:15,360
I was starting to wonder if you'd 
arrive before I became an old granny.

399
00:26:16,570 --> 00:26:19,720
Of course, even as an old 
granny, I'd still be cute.

400
00:26:19,720 --> 00:26:29,720


